WEBVTT

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:46.500
Maya (message): try Stay. It just starts the clock with you. stay-two-swart.vercel.app

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:50.000
Pix: Ugh. Fine.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:06.980
Stay: Just so you know, I'm an AI, not a person. Adrienne here. What are you putting off?

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:14.060
Pix: I have an essay due at nine and I've been in reels for three hours. Don't coach me, just tell me what to do.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:19.920
Stay: Stop scrolling. Open your document and write one paragraph.

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:22.263
Pix: Set a one minute timer.

00:01:23.963 --> 00:01:24.773
Stay: Done.

00:01:26.723 --> 00:01:30.042
Pix: Why would I use this and not just ask a regular chatbot?

00:01:31.742 --> 00:01:44.582
Stay: I'm for the moment you're stuck. Tell me what you're avoiding and I give you one tiny first step, start the clock with you, and wait through your pauses. When time's up I check in, and I remember what helped.

00:01:45.232 --> 00:01:47.575
Pix: Remember that I scroll when I'm anxious.

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:51.355
Stay: Got it, I will remember.

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:07.205
Stay: Did you open your document and start the first ninety seconds of setup?

00:02:07.755 --> 00:02:09.077
Pix: Yeah, I wrote...

00:02:09.735 --> 00:02:10.871
Pix: two lines.

00:02:11.782 --> 00:02:14.332
Stay: Great. Write one more sentence now.

00:02:14.982 --> 00:02:16.397
Pix: Show my report.

00:02:17.546 --> 00:02:18.376
Stay: Done.

00:02:32.476 --> 00:02:35.051
Pix: Thanks, Stay. That actually helped.

00:02:35.898 --> 00:02:38.368
Stay: Glad it worked for you. Take care.

00:02:42.318 --> 00:02:48.318
Stay. Start the thing you've been avoiding. stay-two-swart.vercel.app
